        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your 81-year-old female patient, admitted on 25/07/2014 due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, physical examination revealed decreased air entry bilaterally with diffuse expiratory wheezing. Oxygen saturation was reduced at room air. Diagnostic workup included chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and blood tests, confirming the exacerbation without signs of pneumonia or cardiac decompensation. Treatment consisted of controlled oxygen therapy, nebulized bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. The patient responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. She was discharged on 26/07/2014 with an optimized inhaler regimen and a short course of oral steroids. Please arrange follow-up within two weeks. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
